    {
      "id": "note-two-tone",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 400,
      "text": "The two-tone system\n\nEach partner gets an accent, assigned at pairing: Sam = amber, Alex (you) = teal. Every shared element carries both — the split ring on an alarm row, the paired avatars, the wake receipt. A glance tells you which half is yours."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-ring-hierarchy",
      "x": 470,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 400,
      "text": "Ringing screen hierarchy\n\nThe two big buttons stop YOUR phone only. The \"for both of us\" row is smaller, dimmer, and press-and-hold. Dismissing your partner's alarm by accident is the worst thing this app can do, so that action is deliberate by design."
    }
